<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="webhooks-concept">
  <title>Webhooks Overview</title>
  <shortdesc>PayPal webhooks deliver real-time event notifications to your server
    when payment activities occur — eliminating the need to poll the API.</shortdesc>
  <conbody>

    <p>A webhook is an HTTPS POST request that PayPal sends to your endpoint URL
      when a subscribed event occurs. Your endpoint must return HTTP <codeph>200</codeph>
      within 10 seconds or PayPal will retry.</p>

    <section id="event-types">
      <title>Key Webhook Event Types</title>
      <table>
        <title>Common PayPal webhook events</title>
        <tgroup cols="2">
          <colspec colname="event" colwidth="2*"/>
          <colspec colname="desc" colwidth="3*"/>
          <thead>
            <row><entry>Event Type</entry><entry>Description</entry></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry><codeph>CHECKOUT.ORDER.APPROVED</codeph></entry>
              <entry>Buyer approved the order — ready to capture</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><codeph>PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED</codeph></entry>
              <entry>Capture succeeded — funds collected</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><codeph>PAYMENT.CAPTURE.DENIED</codeph></entry>
              <entry>Capture failed — buyer's payment declined</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><codeph>PAYMENT.CAPTURE.REFUNDED</codeph></entry>
              <entry>Refund processed for a capture</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><codeph>PAYMENT.AUTHORIZATION.VOIDED</codeph></entry>
              <entry>Authorization was voided before capture</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><codeph>CUSTOMER.DISPUTE.CREATED</codeph></entry>
              <entry>Buyer opened a dispute or chargeback</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><codeph>BILLING.SUBSCRIPTION.ACTIVATED</codeph></entry>
              <entry>Subscription became active</entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section id="webhook-payload">
      <title>Webhook Payload Structure</title>
      <p>All webhook events share the same envelope structure:</p>
      <codeblock>{
  "id": "WH-82F81145PK519990L-9BM123456789",
  "event_version": "1.0",
  "create_time": "2024-09-15T10:35:00Z",
  "resource_type": "capture",
  "event_type": "PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED",
  "summary": "Payment completed for $ 220.00 USD",
  "resource": {
    "id": "3C679366HH908993F",
    "status": "COMPLETED",
    "amount": {
      "currency_code": "USD",
      "value": "220.00"
    }
  },
  "links": [
    {
      "href": "https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com/v1/notifications/webhooks-events/WH-...",
      "rel": "self",
      "method": "GET"
    }
  ]
}</codeblock>
    </section>

    <section id="signature-verification">
      <title>Signature Verification</title>
      <p>Always verify webhook signatures to ensure the event originates from PayPal.
        Use the <codeph>PAYPAL-TRANSMISSION-ID</codeph>, <codeph>PAYPAL-CERT-URL</codeph>,
        <codeph>PAYPAL-TRANSMISSION-SIG</codeph>, and <codeph>PAYPAL-TRANSMISSION-TIME</codeph>
        headers with the PayPal SDK or the webhook verification API endpoint.</p>
    </section>

    <note type="warning">
      <p>Never process a webhook event without first verifying the signature.
        Unverified webhooks can be spoofed, leading to fraudulent order processing.</p>
    </note>

  </conbody>
</concept>
